    "surprises": "missed-signal: phase02-installer-not-defensive: simit hooks install did not check for or unset a stale local core.hooksPath that bypasses the canix dispatcher. Phase 04 execution wrote `core.hooksPath = .git/hooks` into all six repo configs (manual or scripted, not by simit or pre-commit). End-result: project hooks fired but AI-strip system step was bypassed. Fixed in verify by `git config --local --unset core.hooksPath` across the six repos. Recommendation for a follow-up: have `simit hooks install` warn (or offer `--fix`) when local core.hooksPath points inside .git/hooks and a friendly dispatcher is the effective system path.\nmissed-signal: projects-scan-skips-entries: skillctl registry entry still reported `hooks: installed` despite no nix/pre-commit.nix on disk; new detector would correct this if `simit projects scan` re-evaluated it (last_seen unchanged from first_seen). Unrelated to hooks-enforcement scope.\nnote: installed simit profile (0.15.2) is stale and cannot parse hooks=\"conflicted\"; phase 04 was executed using /data/nvme0/can/Projects/simit/target/release/simit. Package the new simit release before declaring fleet ready."
